# FRIDAY — line endings are part of the build contract.
#
# GitHub's Windows runners check out with core.autocrlf=true by default, which
# rewrites every LF into CRLF. FRIDAY's contract tests read real source files
# (electron/*.cjs, workflows, scripts) and assert exact multi-line text, so a
# CRLF checkout fails "Run tests" on Windows while passing everywhere else.
#
# Normalizing text to LF in the working tree makes the Windows checkout byte
# identical to Linux/macOS and to what the tests, the audits and the packaged
# EXE expect. Windows-native script formats keep CRLF; binaries stay binary.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.nsh  text eol=crlf

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
*.exe  binary
*.dll  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gguf binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.wav  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.node binary
